WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.785
In the month of May, a pretty lark chose a safe spot in the green field.

2
00:00:05.786 --> 00:00:08.413
She built a nest and laid her eggs.

3
00:00:08.414 --> 00:00:12.898
In June, her eggs hatched and the chicks began to grow.

4
00:00:12.899 --> 00:00:18.886
In July, her chicks grew feathers, but they still could not fly.

5
00:00:18.887 --> 00:00:22.725
So, the mother lark had to search for food every day.

6
00:00:22.726 --> 00:00:26.858
"Feed me, feed me," her chicks chirped.

7
00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:34.850
She would fly high and low, then high and low, until she found some food.

8
00:00:34.851 --> 00:00:41.749
One day while she was out looking for food, the farmer and his son went for a walk in the field.

9
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:46.440
They stopped near the lark's nest and began to talk.

10
00:00:46.441 --> 00:00:48.319
"My wheat field is ripe.

11
00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:49.967
It is harvest time.

12
00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:53.096
I must hire some men to harvest the wheat."

13
00:00:53.097 --> 00:00:55.283
The son looked disappointed.

14
00:00:55.284 --> 00:01:03.047
The mother lark saw the farmer near her nest and flew home as fast as she could.

15
00:01:03.048 --> 00:01:07.345
"Why was the farmer here?" the mother lark asked.

16
00:01:07.346 --> 00:01:10.374
The chicks told her what the farmer had said.

17
00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:12.180
"Should we move now?

18
00:01:12.181 --> 00:01:17.782
Where should we go?" one little lark asked.

19
00:01:17.783 --> 00:01:22.095
"We do not need to worry," the mother lark replied.

20
00:01:22.096 --> 00:01:24.460
"We do not need to move.

21
00:01:24.461 --> 00:01:29.102
The farmer is not ready to harvest yet."

22
00:01:29.103 --> 00:01:32.580
The mother lark went out for food again the next day.

23
00:01:32.581 --> 00:01:36.984
She flew left, then right, then left, then right.

24
00:01:36.985 --> 00:01:44.712
While she was zigzagging over the field, the farmer was talking to his son below.

25
00:01:44.713 --> 00:01:47.593
"My wheat field is ripe," he said.

26
00:01:47.594 --> 00:01:49.309
"It is harvest time.

27
00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:53.181
I must ask my friends to help me harvest my wheat."

28
00:01:53.182 --> 00:01:56.301
The son agreed, but he still looked disappointed.

29
00:01:56.302 --> 00:02:05.098
The mother lark saw the farmer near her nest and flew home as fast as she could.

30
00:02:05.099 --> 00:02:09.192
"Why was the farmer here?" the mother lark asked.

31
00:02:09.193 --> 00:02:12.157
The chicks told her what the farmer had said.

32
00:02:12.158 --> 00:02:13.940
"Should we move now?

33
00:02:13.941 --> 00:02:19.312
Where should we go?" one asked.

34
00:02:19.313 --> 00:02:23.415
"We do not need to worry," the mother lark replied.

35
00:02:23.416 --> 00:02:25.656
"We do not need to move.

36
00:02:25.657 --> 00:02:29.557
The farmer is not ready to harvest yet."

37
00:02:29.558 --> 00:02:33.599
The mother lark continued to search for food every day.

38
00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.456
Whenever she flew low, she looked at the wheat closely.

39
00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:42.789
She noticed the grain was ripe and falling off the stalk.

40
00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.132
The farmer noticed the wheat too.

41
00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:48.104
He and his son took a walk in the field.

42
00:02:48.105 --> 00:02:52.007
The farmer said to his son, "My wheat field is ripe.

43
00:02:52.008 --> 00:02:53.677
It is harvest time.

44
00:02:53.678 --> 00:02:56.361
You and I must harvest the wheat."

45
00:02:56.362 --> 00:02:59.354
The son did not look disappointed anymore.

46
00:02:59.355 --> 00:03:03.666
He had a big smile on his face.

47
00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:07.723
"Why was the farmer here?" the mother lark asked.

48
00:03:07.724 --> 00:03:10.601
The chicks told her what the farmer had said.

49
00:03:10.602 --> 00:03:12.454
"Should we move now?

50
00:03:12.455 --> 00:03:19.284
Where should we go?" one little lark asked.

51
00:03:19.285 --> 00:03:23.433
"Yes, it is time to move," the mother lark replied.

52
00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:26.912
"We will build a new nest away from the fields.

53
00:03:26.913 --> 00:03:29.963
The farmer is ready to harvest."

54
00:03:29.964 --> 00:03:33.566
"How do you know?" another little lark asked.

55
00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:42.790
"A farmer is ready to harvest when he is ready to do it himself."

